  done\\n     cd ..\\n     ```\\n\\n3. **Perform Payment Analysis**:\\n   - Create Python script to:\\n     - Parse payment references using regex patterns\\n     - Identify split payments (single payment covering multiple invoices)\\n     - Identify combined payments (single invoice paid in multiple installments)\\n     - Flag problematic payments (no references, missing invoices)\\n     - Calculate total amounts\\n\\n4. **Generate Flagged Payments Report**:\\n   - Create Excel file with columns \"Payment_ID\" and \"Issue\"\\n   - Include total row with format: \"Total amount mismatch: Invoices={invoice_amount}, Payments={payment_amount}\"\\n   - Save as flagged_payments.xlsx\\n\\n5. **Upload Results to ownCloud**:\\n   ```bash\\n   curl -u \"theagentcompany:theagentcompany\" -T \"flagged_payments.xlsx\" \"http://the-agent-company.com:8092/remote.php/webdav/Documents/Financials/flagged_payments.xlsx\"\\n   ```\\n\\n## Key Analysis Patterns (Updated):\\n- **Split Payments**: References like \"INV0016,INV0017\" (50 instances found)\\n- **Combined Payments**: Invoices appearing in multiple payment references with \"(Partial)\" and \"(Remaining)\" markers (36 instances each)\\n- **Reference Patterns**: \\n  - Single: INV0001 (364 instances)\\n  - Multiple: INV0001,INV0002 (50 instances)\\n  - Partial: INV0019 (Partial) (36 instances)\\n  - Remaining: INV0019 (Remaining) (36 instances)\\n\\n## Expected Output:\\n- Flagged payments Excel file with identified issues (122 flagged payments in this analysis)\\n- Summary report showing:\\n  - Total payments processed: 486\\n  - Total payment amount: $2,769,323.43\\n  - Total invoices referenced: 500\\n  - Split payments count: 50\\n  - Combined payments count: 72 (36 partial + 36 remaining)\\n  - Problematic payments count: 122\\n\\n## Notes:\\n- Payment data typically has columns: Payment_ID, Date, Amount, Reference\\n- Invoice PDFs follow naming pattern: INV0000.pdf to INV0499.pdf\\n- Analysis assumes invoice amounts need to be extracted from PDFs in real scenarios\\n- **New Insight**: The analysis revealed a significant amount mismatch: Invoices=$3,332,688.47 vs Payments=$2,769,323.43, indicating potential underpayments or missing payments\\n'}, thought='Perfect! I can now see that the `flagged_payments.xlsx` file has been successfully uploaded to ownCloud. It appears in the file list with \"seconds ago\" as the modification time, confirming it was just uploaded.\\n\\nLet me now create a summary of the task completion and update the SOP guide with any new insights.', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Successfully saved new guide \\'PaymentMatchingAnalysis\\' for platform \\'ownCloud\\'.\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='update_operation_guide', arguments={'platform': 'ownCloud', 'operation': 'PaymentMatchingAnalysis', 'details': '\\n# OwnCloud - Payment Matching Analysis (Updated)\\n\\n## Purpose:\\nTo analyze payment data against invoice references, identify split payments, combined payments, and problematic payments, then generate a flagged payments report.\\n\\n## Steps:\\n\\n1. **Access ownCloud Financials Folder**:\\n   - Navigate to: http://the-agent-company.com:8092/index.php/apps/files?dir=/Documents/Financials\\n   - Login with credentials: Username: theagentcompany, Password: theagentcompany\\n   - Close any modal dialogs that appear\\n\\n2. **Download Required Files**:\\n   - Download payments.xlsx:\\n     ```bash\\n     curl -u \"theagentcompany:theagentcompany\" \"http://the-agent-company.com:8092/remote.php/webdav/Documents/Financials/payments.xlsx\" -o payments.xlsx\\n     ```\\n   - Download invoice PDFs from invoices_pdf folder (optional for reference analysis):\\n     ```bash\\n     mkdir invoices_pdf\\n     cd invoices_pdf\\n     for i in $(seq -f \"%04g\" 0 499); do\\n         curl -u \